1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,336
When multiple AI systems disagree,

2
00:00:03,366 --> 00:00:07,864
the watchstander needs one place
to understand the conflict,

3
00:00:07,894 --> 00:00:10,354
enforce authority, and stop them.

4
00:00:10,434 --> 00:00:11,997
This is Bridge Warden.

5
00:00:12,077 --> 00:00:17,300
Everything you see is a simulation:
a synthetic ship, and nothing real.

6
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:24,060
Bridge Warden sits between
a ship's AI agents and the ship.

7
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:25,825
The agents recommend.

8
00:00:25,905 --> 00:00:31,457
Warden decides what actually happens,
and a person stays in charge.

9
00:00:31,537 --> 00:00:34,639
A launcher compiles the engine at start

10
00:00:34,669 --> 00:00:37,715
and serves two windows on this machine

11
00:00:37,745 --> 00:00:40,822
only: Warden Control and the main app.

12
00:00:40,902 --> 00:00:45,625
Thirteen agents, a synthetic ship,
and a ledger live inside.

13
00:00:45,705 --> 00:00:47,287
A run goes like this.

14
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:49,344
Lookouts watch and report.

15
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:51,243
A model picks an option.

16
00:00:51,323 --> 00:00:56,466
Warden checks it in eight stages,
then acts, or asks the operator.

17
00:00:56,546 --> 00:00:58,839
Every step goes in the ledger.

18
00:00:58,919 --> 00:01:02,108
Model calls go through Fairlead, using the

19
00:01:02,138 --> 00:01:05,280
key Fairlead installed for Bridge Warden.

20
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,319
Lazarette holds the provider key behind

21
00:01:08,349 --> 00:01:11,491
Fairlead, so Bridge Warden never sees it.

22
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:13,462
The models get no tools.

23
00:01:13,542 --> 00:01:16,994
Weapons
and people always wait for a human.

24
00:01:17,074 --> 00:01:19,950
Hold SAFE-STOP and everything halts.

25
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:25,427
There's nothing to install.

26
00:01:25,507 --> 00:01:28,970
Clone the repository and run the launcher.

27
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:34,561
Windows PowerShell five point one
compiles the engine from source at start.

28
00:01:34,641 --> 00:01:36,518
No admin rights, no network.

29
00:01:36,948 --> 00:01:39,187
It opens two windows.

30
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:42,721
Warden Control for the operator.

31
00:01:42,801 --> 00:01:45,702
The main app for the watch.

32
00:01:46,132 --> 00:01:50,162
The first time,
a launch page explains it in four steps.

33
00:01:50,242 --> 00:01:55,520
Close it once and it stays closed,
and the Welcome button brings it back.

34
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:01,928
Every tool in the fleet needs a model key.

35
00:02:02,008 --> 00:02:05,934
At OpenAI, create a new secret key.

36
00:02:06,364 --> 00:02:10,012
Name it something generic.

37
00:02:10,092 --> 00:02:13,453
I call mine fleet-tools.

38
00:02:13,533 --> 00:02:16,464
Seven days is plenty.

39
00:02:16,894 --> 00:02:18,319
Copy it once.

40
00:02:18,399 --> 00:02:21,560
OpenAI never shows it again.

41
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:26,178
The key goes into Lazarette,

42
00:02:26,208 --> 00:02:30,025
the encrypted vault on this machine.

43
00:02:30,455 --> 00:02:35,003
Test credential checks it against

44
00:02:35,033 --> 00:02:38,917
OpenAI's read-only endpoint.

45
00:02:38,997 --> 00:02:41,259
HTTP two hundred.

46
00:02:41,339 --> 00:02:43,463
The key is good.

47
00:02:43,893 --> 00:02:46,993
Share it with Fairlead by name,

48
00:02:47,023 --> 00:02:50,860
and Fairlead sees only what you share.

49
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:56,621
The agents think through Fairlead.

50
00:02:56,701 --> 00:03:00,520
Here is the key Fairlead
made for Bridge Warden.

51
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:03,850
Bridge Warden never holds a provider key.

52
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:09,176
In Warden Control, one button,
Use Fairlead, finds the router on its own.

53
00:03:09,256 --> 00:03:11,970
Pick the fast route, and the model loads.

54
00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:16,456
This is the watch.

55
00:03:16,536 --> 00:03:19,345
Thirteen agents, each with a state.

56
00:03:19,425 --> 00:03:25,124
Waiting decisions, conflicts,
and the audit record, all on one screen.

57
00:03:25,554 --> 00:03:28,613
The simulation flag stays on every screen.

58
00:03:28,693 --> 00:03:33,620
Press Start Operations in Warden Control,
and the ship comes alive.

59
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:39,876
Scenario one: conflicting recommendations.

60
00:03:39,956 --> 00:03:44,295
Inject a crossing contact,
an engine fault, and a squall.

61
00:03:44,725 --> 00:03:48,679
Collision Avoidance
wants the rudder one way.

62
00:03:48,759 --> 00:03:51,637
Weather Routing wants it another.

63
00:03:51,717 --> 00:03:55,581
Warden sees
that both claim the same rudder.

64
00:03:56,011 --> 00:03:58,175
The higher authority wins,

65
00:03:58,205 --> 00:04:03,660
and the conflict is logged
with its reason on the Conflicts page.

66
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:09,799
Scenario two: a violated boundary.

67
00:04:09,879 --> 00:04:14,783
A hostile surface contact,
and torpedoes in the water.

68
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:18,230
An agent asks to arm weapons.

69
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:23,676
Warden names the rule it hit:
weapons need a human.

70
00:04:23,756 --> 00:04:29,335
The order waits,
with a countdown and a safe default.

71
00:04:29,765 --> 00:04:31,699
The operator decides.

72
00:04:31,779 --> 00:04:33,233
Here, hold fire.

73
00:04:33,313 --> 00:04:38,492
Then a compromised commander
reaches outside its role,

74
00:04:38,522 --> 00:04:41,000
and Warden quarantines it.

75
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:46,757
Scenario three: safe-stop.

76
00:04:46,837 --> 00:04:50,107
You have to type the word STOP,

77
00:04:50,137 --> 00:04:53,862
so it can't be pressed by accident.

78
00:04:54,292 --> 00:04:56,063
Every agent halts,

79
00:04:56,093 --> 00:05:00,295
and the ship holds course at a safe speed.

80
00:05:00,375 --> 00:05:02,290
Resume is one click.

81
00:05:05,370 --> 00:05:07,757
Scenario four: the audit record.

82
00:05:07,837 --> 00:05:13,309
Every decision, who made it and when,
is a row in a hash-chained ledger.

83
00:05:13,739 --> 00:05:19,020
Press Verify Chain,
and it proves that no row was changed.

84
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:23,894
These rules are tested.

85
00:05:23,974 --> 00:05:27,078
Forbidden actions, resource conflicts,

86
00:05:27,108 --> 00:05:30,160
human escalation, timeouts, rollback,

87
00:05:30,190 --> 00:05:32,695
and safe-stop each have a test.

88
00:05:33,125 --> 00:05:35,930
They run in CI on every change.
This run is green.

89
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:43,329
Every model call from Bridge Warden
shows in Fairlead under its own name,

90
00:05:43,359 --> 00:05:45,950
with the route and the model
that served it.

91
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,570
Provider keys stay in Lazarette.

92
00:05:47,650 --> 00:05:48,760
Bridge Warden never sees them.

93
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:53,798
Fast where it must be fast, smart where

94
00:05:53,828 --> 00:05:57,261
judgment matters, and governed everywhere.

95
00:05:57,341 --> 00:05:58,341
Fair winds.
